            },
            "learn": {
                "paragraphs": [
                    "**Postulates** are assumptions specific to **Geometry**.",
                    "**1st:** Straight line from any point to any other point.",
                    "**2nd:** Terminated line (segment) can be produced indefinitely.",
                    "**3rd:** Circle can be drawn with any center and any radius.",
                    "**4th:** All right angles are equal.",
                    "**5th (Parallel Postulate):** If interior angles on same side of transversal < 180°, lines will meet on that side.",
                    "**Playfair's Axiom:** For every line $l$ and point $P$ not on it, there is a unique line $m$ passing through $P$ parallel to $l$."
                ],
                "formulas": [
                    {
                        "rule": "Sum of Angles (Postulate 5)",
                        "formula": "$\\angle 1 + \\angle 2 < 180^\\circ \\Rightarrow \\text{Lines Meet}$",
                        "example": "Condition for intersection."
                    }
                ],
                "boxes": [
                    {
